#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167175 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166938 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74dbd777-f24e-5d23-b495-a56710d71f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08055b09-dc8e-5e64-a169-6b8646c97e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18t-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08055b09-dc8e-5e64-a169-6b8646c97e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18t-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302508} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e093a4e-16c7-597e-9369-a2860151d355" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6dc5997-1d4e-5312-9245-798d648973c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-329817" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}12t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-12t-6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}12t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-2t}\\cdot {e}^{t}-2{e}^{t}\\cdot 2{e}^{-2t}}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & -2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{t}}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & -2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 8t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}-4t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 8t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int -4t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 8t{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=-4t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=-4\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -4t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(-4t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}\\cdot (-4\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}+\\int 2{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(1-2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=8t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=8\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=-{e}^{-t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -4t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =8t\\cdot (-{e}^{-t})-\\int -{e}^{-t}\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8t{e}^{-t}+\\int 8\\,{e}^{-t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8t{e}^{-t}-8{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =-8{e}^{-t}(1+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\ -8{e}^{-t}(1+t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(1-2t)-16(1+t) \\\\ 2(1-2t)-8(1+t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18t-15 \\\\ -12t-6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166937 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6e43401-278c-58f1-b818-fad8546bda0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6e43401-278c-58f1-b818-fad8546bda0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303797} :answer-field/id #uuid "295a6ea8-2810-531b-90a1-1e521e6ec6e3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "596f4cf7-f992-59e0-a1ab-314f9b22d6b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303002} {:answer/id #uuid "5e995f6d-38bc-503f-add8-819490663c94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e995f6d-38bc-503f-add8-819490663c94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496865} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a0f445-2c98-5d5e-9321-6d979dc294b5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dc4c9e61-81e1-5e97-95cb-a89bd2a71a0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-330899" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{t} \\\\ 6{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & -6{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)={e}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{-t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & -6{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{t} \\\\ 6{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot (-6{e}^{2t})-5{e}^{2t}\\cdot {e}^{-3t}}[\\begin{aligned}-6{e}^{2t} & -5{e}^{2t} \\\\ -{e}^{-3t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{t}}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-6{e}^{2t} & -5{e}^{2t} \\\\ -{e}^{-3t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-6{e}^{3t} & -5{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{-2t} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-6{e}^{3t} & -5{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{-2t} & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{t} \\\\ 6{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}12{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 12{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int {e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{4t} \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & -6{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{4t} \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5{e}^{t} \\\\ 9{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166937 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff2cccf5-489b-5e70-b3a9-9d2661562299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365794} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7d0200-75d6-56dc-9a3b-832b6fae8337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c7d0200-75d6-56dc-9a3b-832b6fae8337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496829} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef783e3c-2210-5313-90c8-cc217b3c7be3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "974ddd49-be50-5576-a845-339cab6a2a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4/3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365796} {:answer/id #uuid "0aacdf65-443f-56da-b835-155b66a57197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aacdf65-443f-56da-b835-155b66a57197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496676} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4dc56ff-d11b-5257-828e-dfd7f038bf79" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cab04d20-21da-5031-a5e8-e08eadd456c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-336698" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & -2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & 2{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2{e}^{t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{2}{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"60px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & -2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & 2{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-t}\\cdot 2{e}^{3t}-(-2{e}^{3t})\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2t}}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -2{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & -2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & 2{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166937 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee041e3a-2f24-52a5-bb75-0aca1b12f5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee041e3a-2f24-52a5-bb75-0aca1b12f5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497167} :answer-field/id #uuid "257f025c-7aa8-5698-b6e8-90af2e776c37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5163d8a-75af-5737-80f1-4aea32343cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5163d8a-75af-5737-80f1-4aea32343cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497060} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e897fb2-9841-5b9d-a780-0a38ba920dc8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cbf4a14-013f-525c-b169-07b2a7a14f29" :question/math-academy-id "q-337102" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}},\\,Φ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2{e}^{3t}$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{10}{3}$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-3t}{e}^{t}-0\\cdot {e}^{t}}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]. \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int -2{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 4{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2}{3}{e}^{3t} \\\\ -4{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2}{3}{e}^{3t} \\\\ -4{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]. \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10}{3} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166938 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74dbd777-f24e-5d23-b495-a56710d71f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4c6396-6267-59ce-81e1-3b70290d6465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t+50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c4c6396-6267-59ce-81e1-3b70290d6465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80t+50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496717} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bbf6a85-16be-5ce4-a166-d683ed32df25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497292}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8720bb82-7e04-58ea-82b1-0eeb9a80a59b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337285" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 \\\\ 9 & -8\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}-\\,\\,\\frac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$90t+45$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2{e}^{-2t}\\cdot {e}^{t}-{e}^{t}\\cdot 3{e}^{-2t}}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -{e}^{2t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-t} & 2{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =-[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & -{e}^{2t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-t} & 2{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 15t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int [\\begin{aligned}-5t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 15t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\int -5t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 15t{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=-5t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=-5\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -5t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(-5t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}\\cdot (-5\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}t{e}^{2t}+\\frac{5}{2}\\int {e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}t{e}^{2t}+\\frac{5}{4}{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{e}^{2t}(1-2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=15t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=15\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=-{e}^{-t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 15t{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t & =15t\\cdot (-{e}^{-t})-\\int -{e}^{-t}\\cdot 15\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-15t{e}^{-t}+\\int 15{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-15t{e}^{-t}-15{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =-15{e}^{-t}(t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4}{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\ -15{e}^{-t}(t+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}10(1-2t)-60(t+1) \\\\ 15(1-2t)-60(t+1)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}80t+50 \\\\ 90t+45\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
